  "description": "Install and configure a PostHog SDK in a repository you can read and edit, following PostHog's docs for the framework. Use when a user working in their codebase asks to add, install, or set up PostHog, product analytics, session replay, or a PostHog SDK. Covers finding the right docs page, installing the latest package, getting the project token and ingestion host from project-get, keeping them in the env file, server-side setup, identifying users, and verifying the change. If you can't access the user's code, as is common in ChatGPT on the web or Claude on the web, use installing-posthog-from-chat instead.",
